cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "kwave-power-law-attenuation-calibration"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible numerical audit of power-law acoustic attenuation in k-Wave
  simulations (under MATLAB and CUDA), focusing on two independent sources of
  error: literature parameter transfer and the numerical dispersion singularity
  near y=1. Matching literature linear coefficients to k-Wave's quadratic model
  at 0.5 MHz changes calibration error from -50.13% to -0.97%. Operating near
  y=1 with default dispersion silently induces a -56.8% to -59.4% multiplicative
  attenuation deficit across 0.2-1.0 MHz (R^2 >= 0.999), matching a +57% excess
  in 3-D peak pressure. Approaching y=0.99 leads to 1-D numerical collapse and
  3-D field divergence to order 1e30 Pa across both MATLAB and CUDA backends.
